.TH "PKI \-\-BUNDLE" 1 "2026-09-14" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "strongSwan"
.
.SH "NAME"
.
pki \-\-bundle \- Provides PEM certificate bundle functions
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.
.SY pki\ \-\-bundle
.BR \-\-list
.OP \-\-in file
.OP \-\-debug level
.YS
.
.SY pki\ \-\-bundle
.BI \-\-export\~ selector
.OP \-\-in file
.OP \-\-out file|template
.OP \-\-outform encoding
.OP \-\-reverse
.OP \-\-force
.OP \-\-debug level
.YS
.
.SY pki\ \-\-bundle
.BR \-\-create
.BI \-\-cert\~ -|file
.OP \-\-debug level
.YS
.
.SY pki\ \-\-bundle
.BI \-\-options\~ file
.YS
.
.SY "pki \-\-bundle"
.B \-h
|
.B \-\-help
.YS
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.
This sub-command of
.BR pki (1)
provides functions to work with PEM-encoded certificate bundles.
.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help"
Print usage information with a summary of the available options.
.TP
.BI "\-v, \-\-debug " level
Set debug level, default: 1.
.TP
.BI "\-+, \-\-options " file
Read command line options from \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-l, \-\-list"
List certificates contained in a PEM-encoded certificate bundle.
.TP
.BI "\-e, \-\-export " selector
Export certificates that match the given \fIselector\fR.  This can either be
a numeric \fBindex\fR (use \fI\-\-list\fR to determine it for a specific
certificate), \fBall\fR to export all certificates, \fBroot\fR to export only
self-signed CA certificates, \fBno-root\fR to export all certificates except
self-signed CA certificates, \fBim\fR to export only intermediate CA
certificates, \fBca\fR to export all CA certificates, or \fBee\fR to export all
end entity certificates.
Where certificates are stored is determined by \fB\-\-out\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-o, \-\-out " file|template
Where to store exported certificates. For single certificates the passed file
name is used as is. If multiple certificates are exported, \fItemplate\fR
determines the path where a certificate file is stored to. A unique file name
is generated for each (*-1, *-2, etc.). If a file suffix is missing, then
depending on the value of \fB\-\-outform\fR either .\fIder\fR (the default)
or .\fIpem\fR is automatically appended. If not given, certificates are written
to \fISTDOUT\fR, which forces \fB\-\-outform\fR to \fIpem\fR if multiple
certificates are selected.
.TP
.BI "\-r, \-\-reverse"
When exporting more than one certificate, this reverses their order in the
output (if \fB\-\-out\fR is given it changes the numbering).
.TP
.BI "\-F, \-\-force"
Whether to force overwriting existing exported certificate files.
.TP
.BI "\-f, \-\-outform " encoding
Encoding of the exported credential. Either \fIder\fR (ASN.1 DER) or
\fIpem\fR (Base64 PEM), defaults to \fIder\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-i, \-\-in " file
PEM input file. If not given the input is read from \fISTDIN\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-C, \-\-create"
Create a new PEM-encoded certificate bundle from multiple certificates passed
via \fI\-\-cert\fR. They are added in the order they appear on the command
line.
.TP
.BI "\-c, \-\-cert " file
PEM- or DER-encoded certificate to add to a new bundle. If \fI\-\fR is passed,
the input is read from \fISTDIN\fR. Input may be a PEM-encoded certificate
bundle itself, if so, all certificates are added to the new bundle in order.
Can be used multiple times.
.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.
.BR pki (1)
